From: Oleg Tolmatcev <oleg.tolmatcev@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ls: print the Windows file index for --inode

Windows has no POSIX inode in Metadata, so ls compiled all --inode output
out on that platform.  Use uucore's FileInformation, which opens the path
and combines BY_HANDLE_FILE_INFORMATION's high and low file-index words.
This also gives every hard link to a file the same value.
---
